Chapter: ReverseReverseUnsound

 Stage 5 soundness tripwire for the flagship. The MyCons step of
 reverse (reverse xs) === xs cannot be closed by `cong ih` alone -- the
 goal reduces to reverse (append (reverse t) (MyCons h MyNil)) === MyCons h t,
 which is NOT `f (reverse (reverse t)) === f t` for any f; it needs the
 reverse-append lemma first. Offering only `cong ih` leaves an
 append/reverse mismatch, so the subgoal check must reject with CDX2001.
 If it were accepted, the checker would be unsound.

Section: List

  MyList =
   | MyNil
   | MyCons (Integer) (MyList)

  append : MyList, MyList -> MyList
  append (xs) (ys) = when xs
   is MyNil -> ys
   is MyCons (h) (t) -> MyCons h (append t ys)

  reverse : MyList -> MyList
  reverse (xs) = when xs
   is MyNil -> MyNil
   is MyCons (h) (t) -> append (reverse t) (MyCons h MyNil)

Section: Bad Proof

  claim reverse-reverse-bad : for all (xs : MyList), reverse (reverse xs) === xs
  proof reverse-reverse-bad =
   induction on xs
    is MyNil -> Refl
    is MyCons (h) (t) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "unreachable"
  end
